<title>CHINA: Continental Mariner year net up sharply.</title>
<headline>Continental Mariner year net up sharply.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-08-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended March 31</p>
<p>(in million HK$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (H.K. cents)	 23.4	 vs 5.7</p>
<p>    Dividend (H.K. cents)  5	    vs nil</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	52.16 gain vs 17.13 loss</p>
<p>    Net			  104.44     vs 24.87</p>
<p>    Turnover		   543.68     vs 722.86</p>
<p>    Company name	     Continental Mariner Investment Co Ltd</p>
<p>    Books close		Sept 25-29</p>
<p>    Dividend payable	 Oct 15</p>
<p>NOTE - Continental Mariner is a shipowning and investment holding company. The company proposes a distribution of one bonus share for every five existing shares held.</p>
<p>Exceptional gain represents profit on sale of interest in a subsidiary, and reversal of deficit arising on revaluation of land and buildings.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6368</p>
</text>
